{
  "slug": "zsl-superpowers",
  "name": "Zsl Superpowers",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "An opinionated end-to-end engineering workflow: grill yourself on the spec, write a PRD, slice it into vertical-slice issues, fan out parallel TDD, and ship one consolidated PR. Plus standalone helpers for triage, diagnose, code review, architecture cleanup, and prototyping.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **32 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (32): `ask-zsl` (Interactive router that helps you find the right ZSL skill for what you're doing right now, without leaving…), `codebase-design` (Shared vocabulary and refinements for reasoning about module depth, interfaces, seams, and adapters — the deep-module design language), `decision-mapping` (Turn a loose, multi-session idea into a sequenced map of the decisions and tickets it implies, so it…), `diagnose` (Disciplined diagnosis loop for hard bugs and performance regressions), `domain-modeling` (The home for domain-doc reasoning — the CONTEXT.md Ubiquitous Language format, the ADR format, and the Domain-Driven Design…), `grill-with-docs` (Grilling session that challenges your plan against the existing domain model, sharpens terminology, and updates documentation (CONTEXT.md, ADRs)…), `human-itl` (Walk a human through the manual-action [HITL] sub-tasks of a parent (PRD) issue — the steps a coding…), `improve-codebase-architecture` (Find deepening opportunities in a codebase, informed by the domain language in CONTEXT.md and the decisions in docs/adr/), and 24 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install zsl-superpowers@claude-community` from `ZunoSmartLabs/zsl-superpowers`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "ZunoSmartLabs",
    "url": "https://github.com/ZunoSmartLabs"
  },
